--- body ---
## Context

The raid has an executor-side watchdog (`raid-breaker.py`: 10-minute
stall window, gate heartbeat, `--wait` that wakes the coordinator on
`STALL`/`GATE_TIMEOUT`), but nothing on the coordinator side. An author
who steps away during a raid has no progress trail until the wrap-up
briefing, and a coordinator that went quiet is only noticed by looking.

The author asked for a sitrep every 15 minutes that works on every runtime
the harness supports (Claude Code, Codex, Pi), not just a Claude Code
session cron. A 1-minute idle nudge was considered and set aside: each
wake re-reads the coordinator's whole context (~9M cached tokens/hour at
150K context), and a coordinator with pending background work is already
woken by its notifications and by `raid-breaker.py --wait`.

## Design direction

Split what must be portable from what cannot be:

1. **Sitrep producer, runtime-agnostic.** A script (e.g.
   `scripts/raid-sitrep.py`) that renders the sitrep from durable state
   only: the raid log, git (branches, worktrees, `WAVE_BASE`), the forge's
   open PRs behind `# harness-extension-point`, and `raid-breaker.py`
   readings. Because it reads disk and forge state and no conversation, any
   runtime, the author's own shell (`watch -n 900 ...`) or a system timer can run it.
   Today the raid log has no fixed path (`skills/raid/SKILL.md` mentions it
   at the `WAVE_BASE` step), so this ticket fixes one.
2. **Wake source, per runtime, behind an extension point.** In Claude Code,
   a background command that exits on a 15-minute deadline wakes the
   coordinator, like `raid-breaker.py --wait`. Codex and Pi: find each
   runtime's equivalent; where none exists, the raid prints the sitrep at
   each wave boundary and each circuit-breaker event, and says that the
   timed cadence is unavailable on that runtime.
3. **Fold the nudge into the sitrep.** When the sitrep shows nothing in
   flight and a non-empty queue, the coordinator resumes the next wave
   rather than ending its turn.

Sitrep content (one screen): elapsed time vs. deadline/budget, current
wave and its tickets, each PR's step (executing / gaze / gate round N /
merged / escalated), breakers fired since the last sitrep, the next action.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] The raid log has a fixed, documented path, and the raid writes the
      state the sitrep needs into it.
- [ ] `scripts/raid-sitrep.py` renders the sitrep from durable state alone
      and exits non-zero when it could not read part of its state. It
      never prints an all-clear it cannot distinguish from "could not look".
- [ ] `skills/raid/SKILL.md` arms the 15-minute cadence at raid start and
      disarms it at wrap-up; runtime-specific lines sit behind
      `<!-- harness-extension-point -->` (`scripts/check-agnostic.sh` passes).
- [ ] The per-runtime wake source is documented for Claude Code, Codex and
      Pi. A runtime without one degrades to wave-boundary sitreps, says
      so, and does not fail silently.
- [ ] An idle coordinator with a non-empty queue resumes on the sitrep
      wake (folded nudge); one with an empty queue proceeds to wrap-up.
- [ ] Tests cover rendering from a fixture raid log, the unreadable-state
      exit, and the empty-queue vs. non-empty-queue branch.
- [ ] `make check` passes.

## Raid annotation (Imagine+Plan, 2026-10-27)

**Premise: holds (GO).** On this tree `scripts/raid-sitrep.py` does not exist;
`skills/raid/SKILL.md:196` and `references/circuit-breakers.md:44` say "the raid
log" with no path and no writer; the only wake is `raid-breaker.py --wait`
("Claude Code only", the marker is at circuit-breakers.md:53). No sibling
solved it (main log scanned, no sitrep commit).

**Simplest path.** One stdlib script plus a log convention; no scheduler, no
daemon, no config. Cadence is the runtime's job: Claude Code arms one background
`sleep 900 && raid-sitrep.py` (exits, wakes the coordinator, re-armed each time);
the author's shell uses `watch -n 900`. Antipatterns to refuse: a timer/cron
manager in the harness (YAGNI), a generic "wake source" abstraction with a
plugin API (premature; one marked paragraph per runtime suffices), reusing
`raid-breaker.py` internals beyond a one-shot call (import `classify`, do not fork it).
Codex/Pi wake sources are unverified: the implementer must check once and write
"none found, wave-boundary sitreps" if so (criterion 4 allows it); do not invent one.

**Fixed raid-log path (proposal).** `$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/idh-raid/raid.log`:
append-only text, one line `<epoch> <EVENT> key=value ...` (RAID_START deadline=,
WAVE_BASE sha=, WAVE n tickets=, PR n step=, BREAKER kind=, QUEUE n=). Shared by all
worktrees, untracked (no gitignore edit, no branch-and-PR noise), survives
worktree removal. Env override `IDH_RAID_LOG` for tests.

**Actions (ordered).**
1. Test, then `scripts/raid_log.py` (append/parse helpers, ~40 lines) and the
   documented path; SKILL.md writes RAID_START, WAVE_BASE, wave, PR-step and
   BREAKER lines at the points that already exist (Phase 4 line 196, Phase 5, Phase 6).
2. `scripts/raid-sitrep.py`: render elapsed/budget, wave, PR steps, breakers since
   previous sitrep (last SITREP line), next action; read `gh pr list` (behind the
   extension point, as dashboard.sh does); exit 2 on any unreadable part (log
   missing/garbled, git or forge failure), printing `UNREADABLE <part>` in place of data.
3. Next-action rule in the script: nothing in flight and QUEUE n>0 prints
   `NEXT resume wave`, QUEUE 0 prints `NEXT wrap-up`; SKILL.md says act on it.
4. SKILL.md: arm at raid start, disarm at wrap-up (kill the background sleep);
   per-runtime paragraph(s) behind `<!-- harness-extension-point -->`;
   `scripts/check-agnostic.sh` must pass. Possibly a `references/sitrep.md`.
5. `make check`.

**Files.** New: `scripts/raid-sitrep.py`, `scripts/raid_log.py`, `tests/test_raid_sitrep.py`,
fixture log. Edit: `skills/raid/SKILL.md`, `references/circuit-breakers.md` (path),
generated skills catalog only if frontmatter changes (it should not).

**First failing test.** `tests/test_raid_sitrep.py::test_unreadable_state_exits_nonzero`:
point `IDH_RAID_LOG` at a nonexistent file, expect exit 2 and `UNREADABLE` on output
(no "all clear" string). Then fixture-render, then queue 0 vs n>0 NEXT line.

**Tautological-test check.** Rendering tests must assert on values taken from a
hand-written fixture log (elapsed 25m, PR 12 at gate round 2), not on strings the
script's own formatter produced; the exit test needs a positive control (same
fixture readable, exit 0). The "arms at start / disarms at wrap-up" criterion is
text in SKILL.md: assert the command line and its position under the right
headings (like `test_raid_wave_base.py`), and accept it proves wording only; the
folded nudge is verified through the script's NEXT line, not the prose.
Forge reads must be stubbed with a failing `gh` and a canned `gh` for both branches.

**Shared-file note.** `skills/raid/SKILL.md` collides with 1240 (IDH_ROOT paragraph
at line 15, repeated across skills), possibly 1244 (after-merge runner touches the
Phase 6/merge step) and 1239 (lair, adjacent only via step_clock timings; no
overlap expected). 1237 and 1227 touch gaze/adherence scripts, not raid files:
low risk. Rebase on origin/main immediately before editing SKILL.md; keep the
edits to appended lines and new headings, not the line-15 paragraph.

**Risks.** Codex/Pi wake sources may not exist (degrade, documented); the log is
written by coordinator prose, so a coordinator that forgets a line yields a
sitrep that says "no PR data" (must be UNREADABLE-exit 2, not blank); `gh` rate
or auth failure must also exit 2.

## Raid feasibility (2026-10-27)
